    {
      "id": "p0104-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Although name abbreviations were common in old games localized into English, such abbreviations weren't as pervasive in Japanese-language games - after all, it's easy to say a lot in Japanese with only a few characters. So although the two extra sets of abbreviated names made sense for the English release, there was no strong reason to implement them in the Japanese version.",
        "raw": "Although name abbreviations were common in old games localized into\nEnglish, such abbreviations weren't as pervasive in Japanese-language games\n- after all, it's easy to say a lot in Japanese with only a few characters. So\nalthough the two extra sets of abbreviated names made sense for the English\nrelease, there was no strong reason to implement them in the Japanese version.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28792545,
          0.6521,
          0.90753987,
          0.73818571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28588566,
          0.65138571,
          0.90957965,
          0.73925714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          36,
          37,
          38,
          39,
          40
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "名称缩写在旧游戏的英语本地化中很常见，日语游戏却没有这么普遍，毕竟日语用几个字就很容易表达许多信息。因此，两套额外的缩写名在英语版中有意义，日语版却没有充分的理由照搬。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.29235177,
          0.65067143,
          0.90753987,
          0.74175714
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
